# glyph_sheets.pdl - the Chinese character an ASCII-view cell gets when an events.txt row has NO glyph column (owner 2026-11-18: "these are always supposed to get assigned Chinese characters, not English"; D23).
# SHEET | <sprite sheet stem> | <one Chinese character>. The stem is the sheet name without a leading ! or $ and without trailing digits, compared case-insensitively (People2 -> people, !Door1 -> door, $BigMonster2 -> bigmonster).
# A row with its own glyph column in events.txt always wins. A sheet that is not listed here gets the DEFAULT row (never a Latin letter). Read by _shared-lib/glyph_sheet.c (view_2d_style=ascii in bv_render_2d.c).
SHEET | people | 人
SHEET | actor | 主
SHEET | sf_actor | 主
SHEET | monster | 怪
SHEET | sf_monster | 怪
SHEET | bigmonster | 兽
SHEET | evil | 魔
SHEET | animals | 兽
SHEET | nature | 木
SHEET | vehicle | 车
SHEET | chest | 箱
SHEET | door | 门
SHEET | sf_door | 门
SHEET | flame | 火
SHEET | switch | 关
SHEET | crystal | 晶
SHEET | damage | 伤
SHEET | roof | 屋
SHEET | window | 窗
SHEET | other | 物
SHEET | object | 物
DEFAULT | 物
